{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>On the first day.</b> That day took ten crowns — first for the work of Creation, first for the princes, etc., as is in Seder Olam." "<b>Of the tribe of Judah.</b> Scripture traces his lineage to his tribe — and he did not lift himself above his tribe and bring. Or is it not rather that it says \"of the tribe of Judah\" because he lifted himself above his tribe and brought? Scripture says, \"this is the offering of Nahshon\" — from his own he brought."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:48.885621722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}